<title>ESTONIA: HOIUPANK SHARE HOLDERS' MEETING DETAILS.</title>
<headline>HOIUPANK SHARE HOLDERS' MEETING DETAILS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, the second largest bank in Estonia, said on Tuesday it will hold its general shareholders' meeting on April 12 in Tallinn.</p>
<p>The planned agenda includes a proposal to increase the bank's share capital by 37 million kroons over the next three years and to carry its profit into its reserve to cover previous losses, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Other items for discussion are changes in the bank's inspection board and approval of the 1996 annual report.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
